          heading: "Choices I made",
          body: "I used Astro because most pages only show data, and Astro keeps those pages small and fast. I used React only where a page needs interaction, like the forms, the calendar and the dialogs.\n\nCloudflare Workers runs the app. D1 is the database. Sanity stores the venue data.\n\nThe server builds each booking, so the form cannot change the price or the amount paid.\n\nIn testing, a fake cookie got into the admin area. I fixed it by signing sessions with HMAC. The tests sign cookies the same way the server checks them.",
