        },
        {
          heading: "Bugs the tests found",
          body: "The header crashed when the category request failed. The server sent back an error object, and the header tried to loop over it. Now it only uses the response when it is a list.\n\nThe checkout accepted bad cart items. A zero or negative quantity, or a price stored as text, went straight into the total. Now every item is checked, and bad input gets a 400 error.\n\nA visit to the success page with no cart still saved a $0 order. Now an order is only saved when there is something in the cart.\n\nOrder numbers could come out shorter than the format I wrote down. I switched to a random ID, so they always have the right length.\n\nThe contact email subject showed HTML codes, so a name like Tom and Jerry came through as Tom amp Jerry. Also, a name with a line break could add extra mail headers. The subject now uses the plain name, with line breaks removed.\n\nItems saved from the product grid had no image on the wishlist page. Now the grid saves the image too.\n\nThe contact form could lose a letter when you typed fast, because it used an old copy of the form data. It now uses the latest value.",
        },
        {
          heading: "What I learned",
          body: "The tests that mattered most were on the API routes and the stores, because those hold the rules the screens depend on.\n\nMost of the bugs were at the edges: bad input from the browser, failed network calls, and saved data that did not match what the screen expected.\n\nData saved in the browser needs checks for empty and broken values, because any visit can write to it.",
        },
        {
          heading: "Next",
          body: "The biggest changes I want to make are moving the checkout checks and the pricing to the server, saving orders in the database, and getting lint working again.",
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      eyebrow: "MINIMALIST WRITING APP",
      title: ["KANSO"],
      category: "kanso",
      image: "/images/kanso-mockup.png",
      screenshots: [
        { src: "/images/kanso-mockup.png", alt: "Kanso writing app on a laptop in a library" },
      ],
      summary:
        "A writing app with no dashboard and no big toolbar. Just a page and the few tools you need to write.",
      tags: ["React", "TypeScript", "Vite", "Tailwind CSS"],
      githubUrl: "https://github.com/DeafGecko/kanso-2.0",
      websiteUrl: "https://kanso.09labs.dev",
      caseStudyStatus: "Live",
      caseStudySections: [
        {
          heading: "What it is",
          body: "Kanso is a writing app for people who want to focus. There is no dashboard and no big toolbar. There is just a page and the few tools you need to write.\n\nIt is React and TypeScript, and it has no backend. Your work stays in the browser.",
        },
        {
          heading: "The problem I fixed first",
          body: "The sidebar had two controls for opening and closing it. The button in the header opened it. But once it was open, the close button moved inside the sidebar. The button jumped from the top of the page into the panel, so it was hard to find and close.\n\nI wanted one button in the header that works in both states.",
        },
        {
          heading: "What I changed",
          body: "The header button now opens and closes the sidebar. Its label and icon change with the state. I removed the second close button from inside the sidebar.\n\nI added a pen logo next to the KANSO name. It matches the theme, and it is solid black in light mode. When you hover over it, it plays a short ballpoint click. I made the sound in the browser, so there is no audio file to load. A short delay stops the sound from repeating when you move across the logo and the name.\n\nI also replaced the favicon with the same pen, on a black square.",
        },
        {
          heading: "Contrast",
          body: "The accessibility scan flagged the small labels in the sidebar. I raised their opacity from 40 or 50 percent to 70 percent. The first change missed three label styles, so I needed three rounds before the scan passed.",
        },
        {
          heading: "Tests",
          body: "I used Vitest for unit tests on the header button. I used Playwright for browser tests on desktop and phone sizes. Each browser run also runs an axe accessibility scan, with the sidebar open and closed.\n\nThe tests read whether the sidebar is open before they click, so they pass whether the saved setting opens it or closes it.",
        },
        {
          heading: "The build that was failing",
          body: "The production build was failing before I started. The Vite chunk setting was written as an object, and this version of Vite does not accept that. Vercel runs the same build, so the deploy would have failed too. I changed it to a function that keeps the same three chunks.",
        },
        {
          heading: "How I shipped it",
          body: "Each change went on its own branch. Then I merged each one into main as a squash merge, so the history stays easy to read and each deploy has one clear commit.",
        },
        {
          heading: "Results",
          body: "Vitest passes 2 of 2 tests. Playwright passes 6 of 6, with the axe scans included. The lint check is clean, the production build passes, and the live site scores 100 in all four Lighthouse categories.\n\nI ran Lighthouse on the dev server too. It scored lower there, because the dev server does not bundle the code. The live site is the number that matters.",
        },
        {
          heading: "What I learned",
          body: "I should run the same build command the host runs before I merge. The Vercel build failed on a config error that only showed up once I ran the build myself.\n\nMeasure the live site, not the dev server. The dev numbers looked worse in every category.\n\nWhen you fix a color, search for the color itself, not just one class name. I missed some label styles that used the same color.\n\nCheck small icons at their real size. The pen looked clear at 44 pixels, but the details disappeared at 32.",
        },
      ],
    },
  ],
} = Astro.props;
---

<section class="works" id="works-section" aria-labelledby="works-title">
  <div class="works-header">
    <div class="works-heading-block">
      <h2 class="works-title" id="works-title">{heading}</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="works-hint">{hint}</p>
  </div>

  <ul class="works-accordion" id="worksAccordion">
    {
      [...works].sort((a, b) => Number(Boolean(b.featured)) - Number(Boolean(a.featured))).map((work, i) => (
        <li
          class="slice"
          class:list={[{ "is-active": true }]}
          data-index={i}
        >
          <div
            class={`slice-bg pattern-${work.category}${work.image ? " has-image" : ""}`}
            style={work.image ? `background-image:url(${work.image})` : ""}
          />
          <div class="slice-overlay" />
          <div class="slice-topline">
            <span class="slice-number">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="slice-vertical-label" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="slice-vertical-name">
              {work.title.join(" ")} · {String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="slice-cue" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg class="slice-cue-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="slice-content">
            <p class="slice-eyebrow">{work.featured ? "FEATURED · " : ""}{work.eyebrow}</p>
            <h3 class="slice-title">
              {work.title.map((line) => (
                <>
                  {line}
                  <br />
                </>
              ))}
            </h3>
            {work.summary && <p class="slice-summary">{work.summary}</p>}
            {work.tags && work.tags.length > 0 && (
              <div class="slice-tags">
                {work.tags.map((tag) => (
                  <span class="tag">{tag}</span>
                ))}
              </div>
            )}
            <div class="slice-links">
              <button
                type="button"
                class="project-link project-case-study"
                data-case-study-trigger
                data-title={work.title.join(" ")}
                data-eyebrow={work.eyebrow}
                data-summary={
                  work.summary ?? "Project details are being prepared."
                }
                data-tags={JSON.stringify(work.tags ?? [])}
                data-github-url={work.githubUrl ?? ""}
                data-github-note={work.githubNote ?? ""}
                data-website-url={work.websiteUrl ?? ""}
                data-website-url2={work.websiteUrl2 ?? ""}
                data-website-url2-label={work.websiteUrl2Label ?? ""}
                data-case-study-sections={JSON.stringify(
                  work.caseStudySections ?? [],
                )}
                data-case-study-status={work.caseStudyStatus ?? ""}
                data-screenshots={JSON.stringify(
                  work.screenshots ??
                    (work.image
                      ? [
                          {
                            src: work.image,
                            alt: `${work.title.join(" ")} project screenshot`,
                          },
                        ]
                      : []),
                )}
                aria-label={`Open ${work.title.join(" ")} case study`}
              >
                <FileSearch
                  className="case-study-trigger-icon"
                  size={15}
                  strokeWidth={1.8}
                  aria-hidden="true"
                />
                Case Study
              </button>
              {work.githubUrl && (
                <a
                  class="project-link"
                  href={work.githubUrl}
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noreferrer"
                  aria-label={`View ${work.title.join(" ")} on GitHub`}
                  title="View GitHub repository"
                >
                  <img
                    class="project-link-icon"
                    src="/github.svg"
                    alt=""
                    aria-hidden="true"
                  />
                </a>
              )}
              {work.websiteUrl && (
                <a
                  class="project-link"
                  href={work.websiteUrl}
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noreferrer"
                  aria-label={`Visit ${work.title.join(" ")} website`}
                  title="Open live demo"
                >
                  <img
                    class="project-link-icon"
                    src="/website-icon.svg"
                    alt=""
                    aria-hidden="true"
                  />
                </a>
              )}
              {work.websiteUrl2 && (
                <a
                  class="project-link"
                  href={work.websiteUrl2}
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noreferrer"
                  aria-label={
                    work.websiteUrl2Label ??
                    `Visit ${work.title.join(" ")} (alt)`
                  }
                  title={work.websiteUrl2Label ?? "Open alternate link"}
                >
                  <svg
                    class="project-link-icon"
                    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                    width="18"
                    height="18"
                    viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                    fill="none"
                    stroke="currentColor"
                    stroke-width="1.8"
                    stroke-linecap="round"
                    stroke-linejoin="round"
                    aria-hidden="true"
                  >
                    <circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="5.5" />
                    <path d="M21 2l-9.6 9.6" />
                    <path d="M15.5 7.5l3 3L22 7l-3-3" />
                  </svg>
                </a>
              )}
            </div>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <dialog
    class="case-study-modal"
    id="caseStudyModal"
    aria-labelledby="caseStudyTitle"
  >
    <div class="case-study-panel">
      <button
        class="case-study-close"
        type="button"
        data-case-study-close
        aria-label="Close case study">×</button
      >
      <p class="case-study-kicker" id="caseStudyEyebrow"></p>
      <h3 class="case-study-title" id="caseStudyTitle"></h3>
      <p class="case-study-summary" id="caseStudySummary"></p>
      <div
        class="case-study-tags"
        id="caseStudyTags"
        aria-label="Technologies used"
      >
      </div>
      <!-- screenshot gallery (populated by JS when screenshots present) -->
      <div class="case-study-gallery" id="caseStudyGallery" hidden></div>
      <!-- rich case study sections (populated by JS when caseStudySections present) -->
      <div class="case-study-body" id="caseStudyBody" hidden></div>
      <div class="case-study-actions">
        <a
          class="case-study-action"
          id="caseStudyGithub"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
          aria-label="View on GitHub"
          title="View on GitHub"
        >
          <img
            class="case-study-action-icon"
            src="/github.svg"
            alt=""
            aria-hidden="true"
          />
        </a>
        <!-- shown instead of icon when repo is private -->
        <span class="case-study-github-note" id="caseStudyGithubNote" hidden
        ></span>
        <a
          class="case-study-action"
          id="caseStudyWebsite"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
          aria-label="Visit website"
          title="Visit website"
        >
          <img
            class="case-study-action-icon"
            src="/website-icon.svg"
            alt=""
            aria-hidden="true"
          />
        </a>
        <a
          class="case-study-action"
          id="caseStudyWebsite2"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
          aria-label="Visit alternate site"
          title="Visit alternate site"
        >
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="18"
            height="18"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.8"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="5.5"></circle>
            <path d="M21 2l-9.6 9.6"></path>
            <path d="M15.5 7.5l3 3L22 7l-3-3"></path>
          </svg>
        </a>
        <span class="case-study-status" id="caseStudyStatus" hidden></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</section>

<style>
  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .works {
    width: 100%;
    padding: calc(1.75rem + 10px) 6% 7rem;
    background: #dfe2e3;
    transition: background 0.3s ease;
  }

  :global(.dark) .works {
    background: #0a0e17;
  }

  .works-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 2.75rem;
  }

  .works-kicker {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    font-family: "Azeret Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.6px;
    color: #2a52cc;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }

  :global(.dark) .works-kicker {
    color: #6a9eff;
  }

  .works-kicker .dot {
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    background: #2a52cc;
    display: inline-block;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  :global(.dark) .works-kicker .dot {
    background: #6a9eff;
  }

  .works-title {
    font-family: "Space Grotesk", sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 4.4vw, 3.4rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    color: #454c56;
    margin: 0;
  }

  :global(.dark) .works-title {
    color: #eef4ff;
  }

  .works-hint {
    font-family: "Azeret Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #17377e;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
    max-width: 280px;
    text-align: right;
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
  }

  :global(.dark) .works-hint {
    color: #9bc1ff;
  }

  .works-accordion {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: stretch;
    width: 100%;
    height: min(60vh, 620px);
    min-height: 380px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(42, 82, 204, 0.15);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0.6rem;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    background: rgba(42, 82, 204, 0.02);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  :global(.dark) .works-accordion {
    border-color: rgba(80, 150, 255, 0.15);
    background: rgba(10, 14, 23, 0.4);
  }

  @property --work-border-angle {
    syntax: "<angle>";
    inherits: false;
    initial-value: 0deg;
  }

  @keyframes work-border-travel {
    to {
      --work-border-angle: 360deg;
    }
  }

  .slice {
    position: relative;
    flex: 1 1 0%;
    min-width: 64px;
    height: 100%;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #384351;
    text-align: left;
    font: inherit;
    color: inherit;
    transition:
      flex-grow 0.75s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
      transform 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1),
      box-shadow 0.35s ease;
  }

  :global(.dark) .slice {
    background: #12161f;
  }

  .slice::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 4;
    padding: 1px;
    border-radius: inherit;
    background: conic-gradient(
      from var(--work-border-angle),
      rgba(42, 82, 204, 0.2),
      #5a8eff,
      rgba(42, 82, 204, 0.2) 35%,
      rgba(42, 82, 204, 0.2) 100%
    );
    -webkit-mask:
      linear-gradient(#fff 0 0) content-box,
      linear-gradient(#fff 0 0);
    -webkit-mask-composite: xor;
    mask-composite: exclude;
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .slice:hover,
  .slice:has(.slice-activator:focus-visible) {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.28);
  }

  .slice:hover::before,
  .slice:has(.slice-activator:focus-visible)::before {
    opacity: 1;
    animation: work-border-travel 2.4s linear infinite;
  }

  .slice:has(.slice-activator:focus-visible) {
    outline: 3px solid #5a8eff;
    outline-offset: 2px;
    z-index: 3;
  }

  .slice-activator {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 1;
    padding: 0;
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .slice-activator:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
  }

  .slice.is-active {
    flex-grow: 8;
  }

  .slice-bg {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
    filter: grayscale(1) contrast(1.15) brightness(0.55);
    transform: scale(1.04);
    transition:
      filter 0.6s ease,
      transform 0.6s ease;
  }

  .slice.is-active .slice-bg {
    filter: grayscale(1) contrast(1.1) brightness(0.75);
    transform: scale(1);
  }

  html:not(.dark) .slice-bg {
    filter: grayscale(1) contrast(0.94) brightness(1.02);
  }

  html:not(.dark) .slice.is-active .slice-bg {
    filter: grayscale(1) contrast(0.96) brightness(1.04);
  }

  /* real photos need more light than flat CSS patterns */
  .slice-bg.has-image {
    filter: grayscale(1) contrast(1.05) brightness(0.72);
  }
  .slice.is-active .slice-bg.has-image {
    filter: grayscale(1) contrast(1) brightness(0.88);
  }
  html:not(.dark) .slice-bg.has-image {
    filter: grayscale(1) contrast(0.9) brightness(1.08);
  }
  html:not(.dark) .slice.is-active .slice-bg.has-image {
    filter: grayscale(1) contrast(0.92) brightness(1.12);
  }

  /* generated circuit-like placeholder patterns — swap via the `image` prop */
  .pattern-signalcard {
    background-color: #23262f;
    background-image:
      radial-gradient(
        circle at 20% 30%,
        rgba(120, 150, 200, 0.35) 0,
        transparent 45%
      ),
      radial-gradient(
        circle at 75% 65%,
        rgba(90, 130, 190, 0.3) 0,
        transparent 40%
      ),
      repeating-linear-gradient(
        0deg,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04) 0 1px,
        transparent 1px 26px
      ),
      repeating-linear-gradient(
        90deg,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04) 0 1px,
        transparent 1px 26px
      );
  }
  .pattern-voltfund {
    background-color: #1d222c;
    background-image:
      radial-gradient(
        circle at 65% 20%,
        rgba(130, 160, 210, 0.3) 0,
        transparent 50%
      ),
      repeating-linear-gradient(
        45deg,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 0 2px,
        transparent 2px 22px
      );
  }
  .pattern-kanso {
    background-color: #191d25;
    background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05) 0 1px,
      transparent 1px 34px
    );
  }
  .pattern-factory {
    background-color: #21242d;
    background-image:
      radial-gradient(
        circle at 30% 70%,
        rgba(140, 165, 205, 0.28) 0,
        transparent 45%
      ),
      repeating-linear-gradient(
        0deg,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04) 0 1px,
        transparent 1px 20px
      ),
      repeating-linear-gradient(
        90deg,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04) 0 1px,
        transparent 1px 20px
      );
  }
  .pattern-storyone {
    background-color: #1c2029;
    background-image: radial-gradient(
      circle at 50% 40%,
      rgba(150, 175, 215, 0.3) 0,
      transparent 55%
    );
  }
  .pattern-sift {
    background-color: #20232c;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(150, 175, 215, 0.18) 0, transparent 60%),
      repeating-linear-gradient(
        90deg,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 0 1px,
        transparent 1px 30px
      );
  }
  .pattern-chromatique {
    background-color: #1e1f2e;
    background-image:
      radial-gradient(
        circle at 40% 30%,
        rgba(160, 120, 220, 0.3) 0,
        transparent 45%
      ),
      radial-gradient(
        circle at 75% 70%,
        rgba(90, 160, 220, 0.25) 0,
        transparent 40%
      ),
      repeating-linear-gradient(
        60deg,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03) 0 1px,
        transparent 1px 24px
      );
  }
  .pattern-swiss {
    background-color: #1d2028;
    background-image:
      repeating-linear-gradient(
        0deg,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.045) 0 1px,
        transparent 1px 18px
      ),
      repeating-linear-gradient(
        90deg,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.045) 0 1px,
        transparent 1px 18px
      );
  }
  .pattern-folio {
    background-color: #1a1d26;
    background-image:
      radial-gradient(
        circle at 60% 40%,
        rgba(120, 160, 210, 0.32) 0,
        transparent 50%
      ),
      repeating-linear-gradient(
        45deg,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04) 0 2px,
        transparent 2px 20px
      );
  }

  /* extra tint for bright screenshots where text gets hard to read */
  .pattern-factory ~ .slice-overlay,
  .pattern-chromatique ~ .slice-overlay,
  .pattern-swiss ~ .slice-overlay,
  .pattern-clearcard ~ .slice-overlay {
    background: linear-gradient(
      180deg,
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55) 0%,
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.68) 50%,
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.96) 100%
    );
  }

  .slice-overlay {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(
      180deg,
      rgba(10, 14, 23, 0.15) 0%,
      rgba(10, 14, 23, 0.35) 55%,
      rgba(10, 14, 23, 0.92) 100%
    );
  }

  html:not(.dark) .slice-overlay {
    background: linear-gradient(
      180deg,
      rgba(184, 191, 196, 0.08) 0%,
      rgba(174, 182, 188, 0.34) 55%,
      rgba(163, 172, 179, 0.94) 100%
    );
  }

  html:not(.dark) .pattern-signalcard,
  html:not(.dark) .pattern-kanso,
  html:not(.dark) .pattern-storyone {
    background-color: #b4bbc0;
  }

  html:not(.dark) .pattern-clearcard,
  html:not(.dark) .pattern-factory,
  html:not(.dark) .pattern-sift {
    background-color: #aeb6bc;
  }

  .slice-topline {
    position: absolute;
    top: 1rem;
    left: 1rem;
    right: 1rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
